snippet.textDisplay:
@mikelindinger So to summarize: AI and robots, yes 🤣

But this isn't different to any other 'revolution' we had before (save for the billions of dollars that are being burnt on AI, mind): at one point the technology will hit its limits, demonstrate that it isn't a 'silver bullet', and take its rightful place in our tech stacks. Just remember: robots and AI don't _pay_ for stuff; we do.

My point is that _you can't offset a shrinking population_ , mate. No matter what you do. And from the looks of it, sociologists and demographers are starting to get _really_ concerned, and for good reason: this is going to get _way_ worse. Not for you and me, mind, but how about our future generations?

