snippet.textDisplay:
@dontuse2102 It's not the voting itself that makes the difference. But the idea of consent. "The majority consented to this. This is the will of the people".

Point is, you are fighting the wrong fight. LIBERTY requires no voting. Democracy is about deciding over "commons". Things we share ownership of, like the forests or the city streets. But it is used to legitimize stealing with income taxes for instance. The constitution and declaration of independence are about EQUAL RIGHTS and LIBERTY. They are NOT about 'democracy'.

If people stop accepting that the government claims it has MORE rights than 'equal rights'.... If they stop accepting STEALING in the form of taxes, if they DEMAND liberty, society will recover and market forces will restore wealth. USA became the most wealthy country in the world due to it having liberty. And since it lost that liberty it also lost its wealth. The two go hand in hand and that can be seen all over the world and all throughout history. Countries with more liberty become wealthy.... Even the great empires only became great empires because they afforded their people lots of freedom. When they pulled in the reigns and allowed their people less freedom, taxed them more, wealth was lost and eventually the empires collapsed. It is the same pattern every time.

